{
  "package_id": "SEWCP-300-REQ-001",
  "component": "SEWCP-300_HEATER_PLATE",
  "authority": [
    "spec/02_SEWCP-300_Heater_Plate.md Rev A (FROZEN) - HP-D01..HP-D17, section 2.2 (two-zone spirals: inner r15-72, outer r78-145, 6.00 pitch), section 3.2 (ECR-D-011: >=12 x >=10 keep-out at each kinematic slot, spiral routed tangentially around), section 6 step 3",
    "spec/01_SEWCP-200_Cooling_Plate.md CP-IF-3/CP-IF-4 (choke fasteners and top locators - verified in the SEWCP-200 model)"
  ],
  "scope": {
    "document_name": "SEWCP-300_HEATER_PLATE",
    "units": "mm",
    "bounded": "The heater plate: O300 x 8.000, two-zone heater grooves 3.2 x 3.2 at 6.00 pitch milled into the choke face (inner spiral r15-72; outer spiral r78-145 dodging the three slot keep-outs tangentially), 3x kinematic slots at O260/75-195-315, 16x M5 blind tap drills, lift-pin clearances, He transfer bore, HV bores, the secondary He O-ring groove in the bond face, and the RTD blind bore. Datum: Z=0 at the choke face; bond face at 8.000.",
    "modelling_conventions": "Blind M5 inserts modelled as O5.0 x 6.50 drills from the choke face (HP-D12; 1.50 min to the bond face holds: 8.0 - 6.5 = 1.5). The slot keep-out is the ECR-D-011 >=12 x >=10 rectangle taken as its enclosing disk r=7.81 - conservative. RTD position is not stated by HP-D17: DECISION (design agent) r=40 @ 75, aligned with the cooling plate's RTD-1 column for a shared harness path. HP-D18 edge break and braze details defer to the drawing. HP-08 uniformity is re-verified by thermal map against the as-routed spiral per ECR-D-011's own disposition.",
    "open_state": "No dependency on ECR-Q-011, the CP path-length item, or CP-02. ECR-D-011's thermal-map residual carries."
  },

